flowchart TB
    %% SALIENCE V3 — Autonomous Content Intelligence and Learning
    %% Consolidates ArchV1 / ArchV2 as an extension of implemented ArchCurrent.
    %% Logical responsibilities; boxes are not separate deployment requirements.
    %% Solid: work / evidence flow. Dotted: shared dependencies / control.
    %% All workflows use the existing Temporal adapter and Salience worker.
    %% All transitions persist versioned records, lineage and operation identity.
    %% Governance applies to ALL stages, including retrieval, learning and training.
    %% Detailed contracts, publication states and release flows are in the notes.

    Operator["Operator / API client / CLI / SDK"]
    API["Control API"]
    Goal["Versioned business goal and autonomy limits"]
    Runtime["Temporal adapter and Salience worker"]
    Loop["Intelligence loop: bounded recurring cycles"]

    Operator --> API --> Goal
    Goal -->|committed, idempotent start| Runtime
    Runtime --> Loop

    Intake["Approved sources: intake, provenance and quality"]
    Memory["Scoped retrieval from canonical history"]
    Select["Research, candidates and constrained explore / exploit"]
    Intake -->|untrusted evidence snapshot| Select
    Memory -->|cited experience and current strategy| Select
    Loop -->|goal and pinned run context| Select

    PreCreate{"Creation authorized and budget reserved?"}
    Creative["Creative workflow and built-in AI generator"]
    Build{"Assets, claims, rights and brand pass?"}
    Publish["Publication workflow: final gate, submit, reconcile"]
    Verified{"Remote publication verified?"}
    Select -->|"DecisionRecord and ContentBrief@v1"| PreCreate
    PreCreate -->|allow| Creative
    Creative -->|versioned assets and evaluation| Build
    Build -->|"ReadyToPublishPackage@v1"| Publish
    Publish --> Verified

    Observe["Observation plan and read-only collection"]
    Measure["Versioned outcomes and lineage attribution"]
    Learn["Evidence, hypotheses and failure lessons"]
    Verified -->|"PublicationReceipt@v1"| Observe
    Observe -->|snapshots, completeness and corrections| Measure
    Measure -->|mature outcomes and uncertainty| Learn
    Learn -->|next due cycle while goal is active| Loop

    Change["Versioned strategy or capability candidate"]
    Offline{"Offline evaluation and eligibility pass?"}
    Trial["Capped trial with frozen assignment plan"]
    TrialEval["Experiment evaluation and stopping rules"]
    Promote{"Evidence and promotion authority satisfied?"}
    Active["Strategy and capability release registries"]
    Learn -->|propose, with supporting and contrary evidence| Change
    Change --> Offline
    Offline -->|eligible| Trial
    Trial -->|trial context through normal workflows| Runtime
    Trial -->|logged assignments and exposure| TrialEval
    Measure -->|trial outcomes| TrialEval
    TrialEval -->|continue within existing caps| Trial
    TrialEval -->|completed result| Promote
    Promote -->|promote with receipt| Active
    Active -->|pin strategy and approved capability versions| Loop

    Recovery["Pause, reconcile, bounded rework or escalation"]
    Archive["Archive reasons and evidence in canonical history"]
    Wait["Wait for the next authorized cycle"]
    Select -->|defer or abstain| Wait
    Wait --> Runtime
    PreCreate -->|deny or approval required| Recovery
    Build -->|fail; revision limit applies| Recovery
    Publish -->|final gate denies| Recovery
    Verified -->|unknown, pending or failed| Recovery
    Recovery -->|authorized resume at saved state| Runtime
    Offline -->|fail or unsupported| Archive
    Promote -->|reject or inconclusive| Archive

    %% Shared mechanisms are intentionally shown once instead of at every caller.
    Controls["All stages: identity, policy, rights, brand, budget, audit"]
    Gateway["Typed capability gateway and approved adapters"]
    History[("PostgreSQL records and object-store artifacts")]
    Monitor["Health, cost, data drift and outcome guardrails"]
    Adapt["Provider upgrades or optional curated model training"]

    Controls -.->|authority and stop controls for every workflow| Runtime
    Gateway -.->|versioned model, tool, agent and creative calls| Runtime
    Runtime -.->|every stage persists records and lineage| History
    History --> Memory
    History -.->|rights-cleared dataset versions| Adapt
    Adapt -->|candidate only; no direct activation| Change
    Runtime -.->|workflow and adapter telemetry| Monitor
    Measure -.->|performance and data quality| Monitor
    Monitor -->|breach| Recovery
    Recovery -->|rollback to eligible version or suspend| Active

    %% Canonical persistence includes every learning, archive and release record.
    %% DB-to-runtime handoff uses a transactional outbox and deduplicated consumers.
    %% Every external effect uses stable operation IDs and adapter reconciliation.
    %% Publishing and analytics platforms sit behind their separately scoped adapters.
    %% Active defaults are distinct from candidate and scoped trial eligibility.
    %% A failed gate never advances to a side effect. Rework creates a new version.
    %% A rollback affects future use; published content needs a separate correction.

    classDef runtime fill:#eaf2ff,stroke:#416ca4,color:#182f4a;
    classDef gate fill:#fff4d5,stroke:#a67516,color:#503909;
    classDef intelligence fill:#e6f5ee,stroke:#398369,color:#193f32;
    classDef future fill:#f0eafa,stroke:#8a68a4,color:#45295d;
    classDef store fill:#edf1f5,stroke:#6c8090,color:#253744;
    classDef recovery fill:#fff0e9,stroke:#b3714a,color:#60381f;
    class API,Runtime,Loop runtime;
    class PreCreate,Build,Verified,Offline,Promote gate;
    class Intake,Memory,Select,Observe,Measure,Learn intelligence;
    class Adapt future;
    class History,Active store;
    class Recovery,Archive,Monitor recovery;
